note:
HTTP 200; 12-page PDF of the published article. The quote appears word for word in the abstract. The abstract also confirms:
- the setting: West Midlands, UK, summer 2006 plus heatwave periods in 2006 and 2003;
- the method: a regional weather model, so the results are modelled, not observed;
- 'reduced heat related mortality associated with the UHI by ~25% during a heatwave'.

HTTP 200; 1-page PDF 'Hot Rebates, Cool Savings – Consumer Rebate Program', footer 'Rev 04 2024', for residential customers with active electric service. 'Cool Roofs: up to $0.60 per square feet' was found.

LADWP's current CRP page (www.ladwp.com/crp, which redirects to .../consumer-rebate-program) still lists 'up to $0.60 per sq ft Cool Roofs'. Its details say 'Cool Roof CRP Rebate $0.20-$0.60 per square foot':
- $0.20 at 3-year SRI ≥78 (low slope) or ≥20 (steep slope);
- $0.60 at SRI ≥85 (low slope) or ≥35 (steep slope);
- paid only for roof area over conditioned space.

So $0.60 is the maximum, not a typical rebate.

HTTP 200. The terms quote appears word for word, with 'Updated 17 July 2024'. The Data zip is listed as 351.36 MB in binary units (368.4 MB decimal).

The linked metadata page (_metadata_RDS-2015-0047-4.html) confirms:
- 'published on 12/21/2023' and updated 07/17/2024;
- coverage of CONUS, Alaska and Hawaii;
- 'VALUE = Class (1 = very low, 2 = low, 3 = moderate, 4 = high, 5 = very high, 6 = non-burnable, 7 = water)'.

The county (3,143) and ZIP (32,094) summary XLSX files are in the separate Supplements zip (26.13 MB), not in the 368 MB Data zip.

